SMARTBRIDGE  |  SKILLWALLET
SaveIQ: Smart Savings OS – AI-Powered Personal Finance Dashboard

Project Description :-
SaveIQ is a modern personal finance dashboard that helps users track savings goals, monitor transactions, understand their financial progress and receive AI-powered financial insights. It brings savings missions, transaction management, analytics and an AI financial copilot together in one focused, responsive interface.
The application is a React single-page app built with Vite. A built-in AI Financial Copilot, powered by the Gemini API, reviews the user’s savings progress, goals and recent transactions and turns them into practical next actions shown directly inside the dashboard. Savings missions and transactions are stored in the browser’s localStorage, so the user’s data persists between sessions without needing an account.
The project is hosted on Vercel and its source code is maintained on GitHub.
GitHub Repository:
https://github.com/vedantsakhare/SaveIQ
Live URL (Vercel): [add your Vercel deployment link here]
Problem Statement & Objectives :-
Problem Statement: Many people find personal finance hard to understand and act on. Savings goals are scattered across notes and apps, spending is rarely reviewed, and generic budgeting advice does not reflect a person’s real progress. Users need one simple, free tool that shows where they stand against their goals and tells them what to do next.
The main objectives of the project are:
• Provide a financial dashboard that shows key savings indicators (KPIs) at a glance.
• Let users create Savings Missions and track progress towards each goal.
• Allow users to add and manage transactions so spending and saving behaviour stays visible.
• Present financial analytics that make progress easy to understand.
• Offer AI-generated insights covering progress, risks and practical next actions.
• Persist user data in the browser and provide profile and settings management.
• Deploy the application on a public cloud platform (Vercel) so it works on any desktop or mobile device.
Technology & AI :-
Frontend: React with JavaScript, built and served with Vite
Styling: CSS (App.css) with a modern, fintech-inspired responsive design
Icons: Lucide React
Intelligence: Gemini API, accessed through an API-based integration; the AI Financial Copilot analyses savings progress, goals, recent transactions, savings behaviour and risks
Data Storage: Browser localStorage for savings missions and transactions
Configuration: Environment variable GEMINI_API_KEY kept in a local .env file (never committed)
Code Quality: ESLint (eslint.config.js)
Version Control: Git and GitHub
Deployment: Vercel
System Architecture :-
SaveIQ follows a client-centred architecture. The React application runs in the browser and handles presentation, state management and local persistence. When the user asks for financial insights, the app calls the Gemini API through an API layer so the secret key is not exposed in the interface code. Vercel hosts both the static build and the serverless API route.
