Key Features :-
• Financial dashboard with savings KPIs
• Savings Missions with progress tracking
• Transaction management
• Financial analytics
• AI-powered financial insights through the AI Financial Copilot
• User profile management and application settings
• Persistent browser storage using localStorage
• Responsive interface for desktop and mobile
• Modern fintech-inspired user interface
• API-based AI integration with the key kept in environment variables
Module Description :-
1. Dashboard (Home)
The Home component is the main working area. It shows the savings KPIs, the list of Savings Missions, recent transactions, the analytics view and the AI insights panel, so the user sees their whole financial position on one screen.
2. Savings Missions
A Savings Mission is a savings goal. The user creates a mission and tracks progress towards it. Progress is shown visually and feeds into the dashboard KPIs and the AI analysis. Missions are stored in localStorage.
3. Transaction Management
Users record and manage transactions. The transaction history keeps spending and saving behaviour visible and is used for the analytics and for the AI Copilot’s review of recent activity. Transactions are stored in localStorage.
4. Financial Analytics
The analytics module summarises savings progress and transaction activity so users can understand trends and how close they are to their goals.
5. AI Financial Copilot
The AI Financial Copilot evaluates six areas and presents the result inside the application:
• Savings progress
• Financial goals
• Recent transactions
• Savings behaviour
• Potential risks
• Practical next actions
The Gemini API key is supplied through the GEMINI_API_KEY environment variable and must never be committed to GitHub.
6. Profile and Settings
The Profile component manages user details and the Settings component manages application preferences. A StepGuide component walks first-time users through the main steps of using SaveIQ.
Scenarios :-
Scenario 1: A student creates a Savings Mission for a laptop, adds a few transactions and watches the dashboard KPIs and mission progress update immediately.
Scenario 2: A user records several spending transactions and opens Analytics to see how their activity compares with their savings goals.
Scenario 3: A user requests AI insights and receives an assessment of progress, risks and practical next actions based on their goals and recent transactions.
Scenario 4: A returning user closes the browser and comes back later; missions and transactions are restored from localStorage.
Milestones :-
Milestone 1 – Project Planning & UI/UX Design
Define the goal of SaveIQ, finalize the dashboard, missions, transactions, analytics and AI modules, and design the fintech-inspired interface.
Milestone 2 – Frontend Development
Set up React with Vite and build the Home, Profile, Settings and StepGuide components with responsive CSS and Lucide icons.
Milestone 3 – Core Features & Persistence
Implement Savings Missions, transaction management and analytics, with data saved in localStorage.
Milestone 4 – AI Integration
Integrate the Gemini API through the API layer to power the AI Financial Copilot, with the key stored in environment variables.
Milestone 5 – Testing, Optimization & Deployment
Test the features on desktop and mobile, run lint and build checks, and deploy the final application on Vercel.
Deployment on Vercel :-
SaveIQ is deployed on Vercel from the GitHub repository, so a push to the main branch can trigger a new deployment.
Live URL (Vercel): [add your Vercel deployment link here]
• Step 1: Push the SaveIQ project to a GitHub repository.
• Step 2: On Vercel, choose Add New > Project and import the repository.
• Step 3: Vercel detects the Vite framework; the Build Command is “npm run build”.
• Step 4: Add the GEMINI_API_KEY environment variable in the project settings.
• Step 5: Click Deploy. Vercel builds the project and publishes it over HTTPS.
• Step 6: Open the URL, create a mission, add a transaction and test the AI insights.
