Security & Limitations :-
Security measures: The Gemini API key is held in an environment variable, .env files are excluded from the repository through .gitignore, and Vercel serves the app over HTTPS.
The current limitations are:
• Data is stored in browser localStorage, so it is limited to one browser and device and is lost if the browser data is cleared.
• There is no user authentication yet, so the app is single-user per browser.
• AI insights depend on the Gemini API being available and on a valid API key.
• AI output is guidance only and is not professional financial advice.
• Charts are basic; advanced financial charts are planned.
• Transactions are entered manually; recurring transactions are not automated yet.
Future Scope :-
• Advanced financial charts
• User authentication
• Cloud database synchronization across devices
• Automated recurring transactions
• Budget categories
• Exportable financial reports
• Notifications and goal reminders
• More advanced AI financial planning
Conclusion :-
SaveIQ turns personal finance into something simple to understand, track and act on. By combining savings missions, transaction tracking, analytics and an AI Financial Copilot in a responsive React dashboard deployed on Vercel, the project demonstrates frontend development, application state management, responsive UI design, API integration and AI-powered features. Its modular component structure leaves clear room for authentication, cloud sync and richer AI planning.
Expected Outcome :-
SaveIQ aims to help everyday users build better saving habits by giving them clear visibility of their goals and spending, plus actionable AI guidance, from any device through a public link.
